1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:20,982
This video shows the third way to control the player. It is imperative control, with the API ref property. Unlike the previous video, your code doesn't describe a state. It calls the player directly, one command at a time, and some things, like speed, work only this way.

2
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,392
First, we need a handle to the player. Let's create a ref for it.

3
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:36,001
The ref starts empty. It will hold the player once the player is on the page.

4
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:41,126
Now let's add the player in a card, and pass it that ref.

5
00:00:52,900 --> 00:01:00,554
The API ref property fills the ref with the player. There is no autoplay here, so nothing plays until we call it.

6
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:07,939
Now the commands. Let's add a Play button and a Pause button, each calling the player.

7
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:24,079
Each button calls one method on the player, play or pause.

8
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:27,991
Let's press Play, and then Pause.

9
00:01:32,533 --> 00:01:36,713
It plays, and then stops right where it was, until the next call.

10
00:01:37,933 --> 00:01:43,315
To jump back to the beginning, we set the time to zero. Let's add a Restart button.

11
00:01:53,133 --> 00:01:57,679
Set current time takes milliseconds, so zero is the very start.

12
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:01,303
Let's press Play, and then Restart.

13
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,086
It jumps back to the start, and keeps playing.

14
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:13,879
To show any moment, let's add a slider that sets the player's progress.

15
00:02:25,333 --> 00:02:30,218
Set current progress takes a number from zero to one, and the player jumps there.

16
00:02:31,467 --> 00:02:32,512
Let's drag it.

17
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:41,536
Each move of the slider is one call, and the ball follows it.

18
00:02:42,767 --> 00:02:48,409
Speed is a command too. Let's add a button for double speed, and one that plays backwards.

19
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:09,596
Set playback rate changes the speed. Two is twice as fast, and minus one plays in reverse.

20
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:16,476
Let's press Play, then double speed, then Reverse, and finally Pause.

21
00:03:22,367 --> 00:03:28,610
Twice as fast, and then backwards. Each button is one call, and the player does exactly that.

22
00:03:29,833 --> 00:03:40,805
So, with the API ref property, your code commands the player directly. Play, pause, jump to any moment, and change the speed, each with a single call.
